      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`DecodeBenchConnector` fills a new request's own blocks in every KV cache group, like a P/D transfer, but it inherits the base `get_loaded_kv_cache_group_ids`, which reports only the prefix-cacheable groups (what a hash-addressed store holds). A bounded-replay sliding-window group (DeepSeek V4.1) is not prefix-cacheable, so the scheduler treats the window as not loaded and replays it on the first step of every filled request. That step becomes a mixed prefill step instead of a padded decode, and with DP it pulls every rank out of the FULL decode graph, so decode-only benchmarks with this connector do not reflect P/D decode.\n\nThis returns `transfer_group_ids`, the same as `NixlConnector` and `MooncakeConnector`.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- New `test_decode_bench_connector_loads_bounded_replay_groups`: a full-attention group plus a bounded-replay `SlidingWindowMLASpec` group; the connector must report both groups. It fails without the fix (`(0,) == (0, 1)`).\n- `pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_decode_bench_connector.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_replay.py`\n\n## Test Result\n\n44 passed (30 in test_decode_bench_connector.py, 14 in test_prefix_replay.py).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
